00:27:27,679 --> 00:27:37,590
which is a fairly common spatial operation where you take the area of the intersection of the two polygons divided by the area of the union of the two polygons

271
00:27:37,590 --> 00:27:45,830
and you get this ratio that compares the do polygons similarity essentially and depending on the value of

272
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:53,190
that and we set various thresholds we will then say this is the same building and therefore and that next release it will have

273
00:27:53,190 --> 00:28:00,950
that same g ID and so that's how we achieve stability over time across releases with our gers ID system is based on the quality of our matchers

